# 3awedlou — Mosquitto ACL (development).
#
# RULE: the broker username of a machine MUST equal the identifier that the
#       backend puts in the topic, i.e. Machine.identifier ("3awedlou-001"),
#       NOT the machine UUID. bin/mqtt-user.ps1 enforces that you pass such a
#       name; acl patterns (%u = authenticated username) then pin every
#       device to its own topic branch.
#
# "3awedlou" below is the default MQTT_PREFIX. If you change MQTT_PREFIX you
# MUST change every occurrence here too, otherwise the backend user and the
# devices will be authorised against topics nobody publishes to.
#
# After editing this file: docker compose -f compose.mqtt.yaml restart mosquitto

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- backend ----
# The Symfony backend (publisher + app:mqtt:consume) needs the whole tree:
# read the telemetry/status/events it consumes and write the commands it
# publishes.
user backend
topic readwrite 3awedlou/#

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- machines ----
# Each device: write its OWN telemetry/status/events, read only its OWN
# command topic. Publishing to another machine's topic matches no rule and is
# denied (Mosquitto denies when nothing matches).
pattern write 3awedlou/machines/%u/telemetry
pattern write 3awedlou/machines/%u/status
pattern write 3awedlou/machines/%u/events
pattern read 3awedlou/machines/%u/commands
